course: dictionary
lesson: 9026
title: Slabs and context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A slab is a thick, flat piece of something hard, like stone, concrete or wood. You do not always need a dictionary: read the words around it. «Ancient builders moved a heavy stone slab with a crowbar and ramps.» Heavy, crowbar and ramps are clues that a slab is big, hard and difficult to lift.
explain: Slab can also mean a thick, flat piece of food, such as «a slab of cake». The words thick and flat are the clues here, because they describe the shape. Think of a slab as a shape first, and then ask what it is made of.
explain: Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The path was made of paving slabs.» If you swap in thin and round, like a coin, it does not fit a path. Thick and flat stone pieces do fit, so that is the right meaning.
fact: A slab is a thick, flat piece of something hard, like stone, concrete or wood.
fact: A slab of food, such as «a slab of cake» or chocolate, is a thick, flat piece of it.
fact: In building, a slab is a flat concrete floor or base.
fact: The outer shell of the Earth is broken into huge slabs called plates, which move a few centimetres a year.
fact: In maths, a slab is shaped like a cuboid, so you can work out its area or volume.
exercise: «A slab of stone covered the secret tunnel.» What is a slab? | *A thick, flat piece of something hard | A thin, round piece of paper | A tall tree trunk | A soft, wet cloud
exercise: «She cut a big slab of chocolate for everyone.» What does slab mean here? | *A thick, flat piece of food | A bar of soap | A small drop of juice | A long, thin stick
exercise: In building, what is a slab? | A pointed roof | *A flat concrete floor or base | A hole dug in the ground | A tall wall of bricks
test: «The outer shell of the Earth is broken into huge slabs called plates.» What do the slabs look like? | Thin and round like coins | *Huge, thick and flat | Tiny like grains of sand | Soft and wet like mud
test: In maths, a slab is shaped like a cuboid. What shape is a cuboid? | A flat circle | A ball | A cone | *A box shape with flat faces
exam: «Ancient builders moved a stone slab with a crowbar and ramps.» What does this tell you about a slab? | *It is heavy and needs tools to move | It is always made of wood | It is light enough to carry in one hand | It floats on water
